WEBVTT

00:01.918 --> 00:03.503
<i>After receiving a request for help,</i>

00:03.586 --> 00:06.381
<i>America's number one hero,
Star and Stripe,</i>

00:06.464 --> 00:08.008
<i>arrived in Japan.</i>

00:08.508 --> 00:11.636
<i>Tomura Shigaraki attacked her right away.</i>

00:13.263 --> 00:15.974
<i>Star used her Quirk, New Order,
which allowed her</i>

00:16.057 --> 00:17.517
<i>to apply rules to nature.</i>

00:17.600 --> 00:18.977
<i>She cornered Shigaraki,</i>

00:19.936 --> 00:22.605
<i>but Shigaraki defeated her
by the skin of his teeth.</i>

00:23.732 --> 00:25.150
<i>But it was revealed later on</i>

00:25.233 --> 00:26.693
<i>that Star used the last moments</i>

00:27.485 --> 00:28.611
<i>of her life</i>

00:28.695 --> 00:32.115
<i>to cause extensive damage
to Shigaraki's Quirks.</i>

00:33.575 --> 00:35.118
Shigaraki will be immobile

00:35.201 --> 00:36.995
for at least a week.

00:37.078 --> 00:40.957
It's the gift of time that Star and Stripe
left behind for us.

00:41.833 --> 00:43.168
In order to protect yourselves

00:43.251 --> 00:45.795
and everything you consider dear,

00:46.379 --> 00:50.383
I want you all to use this time
we've been given to power up.

00:53.219 --> 00:56.931
ORIGINAL STORY BY KOHEI HORIKOSHI

02:32.944 --> 02:35.947
It's okay, my other self.

02:36.614 --> 02:37.615
No worries.

02:38.491 --> 02:41.953
The factors within you are
in a melee, causing you to break down.

02:42.787 --> 02:46.666
Give it some time, and you'll be able
to use your Quirks again.

02:47.375 --> 02:51.087
I'll kill them. I'm going to kill them!

02:51.170 --> 02:52.171
I hate them!

02:53.172 --> 02:57.135
As long as even one person remembers
All Might's face,

02:57.218 --> 02:59.470
this anger will not dissipate!

03:00.054 --> 03:02.807
<i>Our minds are fusing together.</i>

03:03.391 --> 03:04.934
<i>I can feel it...</i>

03:05.643 --> 03:07.770
<i>His boiling anger.</i>

03:07.854 --> 03:11.524
<i>I can feel Tomura's hatred now.</i>

03:12.525 --> 03:13.568
Don't worry.

03:14.319 --> 03:15.612
You're doing good.

03:16.529 --> 03:18.740
<i>We couldn't get New Order,</i>

03:18.823 --> 03:22.619
<i>but we also got rid
of a very big obstacle.</i>

03:23.244 --> 03:24.913
So we can relax a little.

03:24.996 --> 03:28.708
Clinging on to one particular plan
is not a good thing.

03:30.209 --> 03:33.546
I know you've been preparing,
so I'm sorry to have to say this,

03:33.630 --> 03:35.298
but stay put for a little longer.

03:35.882 --> 03:39.886
No way. I've reached my limit.
My dad is flying around as we speak.

03:39.969 --> 03:41.304
I can't stand it.

03:41.888 --> 03:43.514
Toya.

03:43.598 --> 03:47.185
You and I are alike,
but we have one major difference.

03:48.561 --> 03:49.479
Listen up.

03:50.396 --> 03:54.776
I devise many, many possible routes
in advance

03:54.859 --> 03:58.446
to reach the goal I have in mind.

03:59.280 --> 04:04.077
<i>Strictly speaking, I plan out
numerous possible routes,</i>

04:04.160 --> 04:07.288
<i>years and dozens of years in advance,</i>

04:07.372 --> 04:12.377
<i>and I choose the best route among them
to reach my goal.</i>

04:13.044 --> 04:13.878
That's right.

04:14.545 --> 04:16.256
There are countless routes.

04:17.840 --> 04:20.885
<i>The completion of the perfect body
has been put on pause,</i>

04:20.969 --> 04:25.223
<i>and Izuku Midoriya has returned
to the security of the UA,</i>

04:26.057 --> 04:28.810
<i>but unlike you, Toya,</i>

04:29.352 --> 04:31.479
<i>I have lots of friends.</i>

04:39.320 --> 04:40.488
Go, my birds!

04:41.572 --> 04:42.782
I'll get you!

04:42.865 --> 04:44.200
Black Abyss.

04:45.660 --> 04:47.245
Come at me!

04:49.122 --> 04:50.957
Octoblow!

04:51.040 --> 04:52.583
Tornado Tail Dance.

04:56.379 --> 04:59.215
- Chargebolt!
- Here it goes!

05:01.592 --> 05:04.387
Take this!

05:06.139 --> 05:07.265
One more time!

05:07.974 --> 05:10.059
- Froppy!
- Uravity!

05:10.643 --> 05:12.562
- Meteor...
- Fafrotskies!

05:15.523 --> 05:16.774
Blackwhip!

05:18.901 --> 05:20.111
Eat this!

05:23.406 --> 05:24.490
<i>I got him!</i>

05:27.535 --> 05:29.203
Take this!

05:34.375 --> 05:38.171
I learned from Endeavor
about building up and releasing.

05:38.254 --> 05:40.089
Instead of using it in one blast,

05:40.173 --> 05:43.551
<i>I'll change it into beads of sweat
and use it in simultaneous blasts.</i>

05:43.634 --> 05:45.887
<i>That's my new skill, Cluster.</i>

05:45.970 --> 05:49.849
All of my techniques
will be more powerful,

05:49.932 --> 05:52.435
although it does take time
to warm up my body.

05:53.269 --> 05:54.896
That's why you're bundled up.

05:54.979 --> 05:58.024
The heat drains me of stamina,
but I have to choose one or the other.

05:58.816 --> 05:59.776
Todoroki

06:00.359 --> 06:03.071
seems a little different too.

06:04.030 --> 06:06.032
I've barely gotten the hang of it.

06:06.657 --> 06:09.786
<i>But I think I'm able to control
my left side as well as my right.</i>

06:10.578 --> 06:12.371
<i>I can't let Dabi burn me alive.</i>

06:16.959 --> 06:19.754
My left side and right side make one body.

06:24.300 --> 06:26.719
All Might said that it'll become
an all-out battle.

06:26.803 --> 06:27.804
Yeah?

06:27.887 --> 06:31.099
But the top two villains are
in a vulnerable state, right?

06:31.766 --> 06:35.436
<i>Gigantomachia has been
detained and sedated, right?</i>

06:35.520 --> 06:38.898
If we can find the top two villains,
we'd be able to end things, no?

06:38.981 --> 06:40.650
There are three reasons why you're wrong.

06:40.733 --> 06:42.568
What? Three?

06:43.152 --> 06:45.696
First of all, we probably
won't be able to find them.

06:46.364 --> 06:48.116
<i>So far, we found the Nomu hangar,</i>

06:48.199 --> 06:51.410
<i>Shigaraki's hideout,
and the research facility,</i>

06:51.953 --> 06:57.125
<i>but we haven't been able to track down
the boss after his defeat by All Might.</i>

06:57.208 --> 06:59.752
No one's better than him
when it comes to hiding,

07:00.336 --> 07:01.796
that nut head.

07:01.879 --> 07:03.005
Don't talk dirty.

07:03.631 --> 07:04.465
Secondly,

07:05.299 --> 07:07.385
<i>during the last battle with Shigaraki,</i>

07:07.468 --> 07:09.720
<i>his body was not complete.</i>

07:10.888 --> 07:14.016
<i>And when considering
the enormous decline in our forces,</i>

07:14.100 --> 07:16.769
we are, at best,
50% of the size we used to be.

07:16.853 --> 07:17.687
True that.

07:18.563 --> 07:19.689
And thirdly,

07:20.523 --> 07:23.359
they're the ones who'll choose
when to begin the battle.

07:23.943 --> 07:25.486
<i>The Search Quirk,</i>

07:25.570 --> 07:28.781
<i>which allows Quirks to be detected
from afar, was stolen from Ragdoll.</i>

07:29.532 --> 07:32.201
<i>Even if that Quirk disappeared
during the fight against the US,</i>

07:32.785 --> 07:34.787
<i>their next attack is inevitable.</i>

07:35.371 --> 07:38.666
That's why we're trying to gather
as much manpower as we can.

07:40.626 --> 07:42.503
But we can choose
how to enter this battle,

07:42.587 --> 07:46.883
to lure Shigaraki in a way that's
advantageous to us. I'll go search too...

07:46.966 --> 07:49.260
"We'll go search," right?

07:51.429 --> 07:53.389
That's right, Midoriya!

08:02.940 --> 08:03.774
Yeah.

08:06.194 --> 08:08.613
Oh, that reminds me,

08:08.696 --> 08:10.573
I can walk around, right?

08:10.656 --> 08:12.241
To a certain degree.

08:12.325 --> 08:14.619
After Uraraka's speech,

08:14.702 --> 08:18.039
the tension between the Hero Class
and the evacuees has been reduced.

08:19.790 --> 08:20.708
In the end,

08:21.542 --> 08:24.253
no matter how much we push
All For One into a corner,

08:25.880 --> 08:27.215
he continues to laugh.

08:30.426 --> 08:32.595
<i>Ever since that Gunga and Jaku
battle ended,</i>

08:33.262 --> 08:34.639
<i>you've been feeling down.</i>

08:35.640 --> 08:37.767
<i>Everyone was feeling down, but...</i>

08:38.684 --> 08:40.561
You have no choice but to do it.

08:40.645 --> 08:43.147
He sent another order.

08:43.689 --> 08:45.816
It's okay. It's coded as always,

08:45.900 --> 08:50.363
so even if it's intercepted, it'll look
like messages between civilians.

08:50.446 --> 08:53.115
The security cameras
won't catch us here, right?

08:53.908 --> 08:55.034
It's okay.

08:55.535 --> 08:57.870
<i>Even after Midoriya came back,</i>

08:58.496 --> 09:01.457
<i>you never smiled, so that got me worried.</i>

09:01.958 --> 09:04.293
You did everything All For One ordered

09:04.377 --> 09:06.295
up until the Kamino incident.

09:06.379 --> 09:09.215
You have to do it, or we'll get killed,

09:10.132 --> 09:11.425
Yuga!

09:12.552 --> 09:14.387
Right after you entered this academia,

09:14.470 --> 09:16.806
you did what he told you to do.

09:16.889 --> 09:21.310
Even during the training camp, you leaked
the location without anyone noticing!

09:22.812 --> 09:25.565
<i>The villains that suddenly appeared
at the USJ...</i>

09:26.274 --> 09:27.858
<i>Same with the Forest Training Camp...</i>

09:27.942 --> 09:29.402
<i>The location was a secret,</i>

09:29.986 --> 09:31.362
<i>but the villains found us.</i>

09:32.238 --> 09:33.155
<i>Don't tell me...</i>

09:33.656 --> 09:38.244
Never even once
did we do this because we wanted to!

09:38.327 --> 09:42.456
But it's too late to back out now!

09:43.332 --> 09:45.167
Mama. Papa.

09:45.960 --> 09:48.212
But I...

09:49.088 --> 09:52.633
<i>No way! You've got to be kidding me!
I can't believe it!</i>

09:52.717 --> 09:55.428
<i>Aoyama is... Aoyama...</i>

09:56.012 --> 10:01.225
We just wanted you to be happy.

10:01.309 --> 10:04.061
<i>Do you want to be like
everyone else, Yuga?</i>

10:04.145 --> 10:05.062
<i>Yeah.</i>

10:05.146 --> 10:09.525
<i>Because it's scary
to be different from others.</i>

10:10.109 --> 10:14.322
<i>You were born Quirkless,
but we wanted you to fit in</i>

10:15.114 --> 10:17.658
<i>and chase after your dreams with everyone!</i>

10:18.659 --> 10:20.620
That's all we wanted for you.

10:23.080 --> 10:26.459
We would've never done it if we knew
that this is how it would become.

10:26.542 --> 10:31.213
We would've never
asked All For One to give you a Quirk!

10:31.297 --> 10:33.299
But now that

10:34.467 --> 10:36.927
<i>we've dealt with him,</i>

10:37.011 --> 10:39.388
<i>we can never get away from All For One!</i>

10:42.058 --> 10:42.892
<i>Somebody!</i>

10:42.975 --> 10:44.143
<i>I need to call a teacher!</i>

10:45.770 --> 10:48.022
It's been so hard and painful.

10:48.981 --> 10:52.360
I've done my part
to not attract suspicion.

10:53.069 --> 10:55.154
I was overwhelmed with guilt,

10:56.614 --> 10:58.866
so I put on a brave face!

11:00.785 --> 11:02.995
<i>When All For One was captured at Kamino,</i>

11:04.121 --> 11:07.750
<i>I was selfish and got the wrong idea...</i>

11:08.668 --> 11:10.753
that I could finally be together
with everyone.

11:11.337 --> 11:14.507
Yuga! Forgive us!

11:14.590 --> 11:16.634
Forgive us for being such fools.

11:16.717 --> 11:17.802
I...

11:17.885 --> 11:19.804
wanted to protect you both, Mama and Papa.

11:20.721 --> 11:22.431
I didn't want you two to die.

11:23.349 --> 11:24.558
Yuga,

11:24.642 --> 11:28.396
please help us.

11:28.479 --> 11:29.688
Yuga!

11:39.740 --> 11:41.826
Um... I...

11:42.535 --> 11:43.661
heard from Hagakure...

11:44.370 --> 11:46.455
about a traitor...

11:47.456 --> 11:51.043
What could you be talking about?
I'm sure it was a misunderstanding!

11:52.670 --> 11:54.171
Midoriya.

11:55.381 --> 11:56.674
Midoriya.

11:57.925 --> 11:58.801
<i>Back then,</i>

11:59.677 --> 12:01.971
<i>I was the only one
who couldn't say anything...</i>

12:03.389 --> 12:07.184
<i>while everyone
spoke up to say something to you...</i>

12:08.185 --> 12:11.272
<i>while everyone was desperately
trying to help you...</i>

12:12.440 --> 12:15.109
<i>At that moment,
I was the only one who couldn't...</i>

12:17.111 --> 12:18.779
Aoyama, I...

12:19.363 --> 12:20.739
Stop it!

12:21.282 --> 12:22.575
My power

12:23.159 --> 12:27.121
is a special power that I received
from All Might.

12:27.705 --> 12:28.539
<i>You...</i>

12:29.290 --> 12:32.293
I've always wanted to be
on equal footing with you.

12:32.877 --> 12:34.170
<i>You...</i>

12:34.253 --> 12:35.546
I...

12:36.255 --> 12:39.258
noticed that you were looking
really gloomy,

12:40.301 --> 12:43.596
so I was worried about you,
and that's why I came to look for you.

12:46.182 --> 12:47.183
<i>Yes,</i>

12:48.642 --> 12:49.894
<i>I was the only one...</i>

12:54.398 --> 12:56.734
At the USJ and at the training camp...

12:56.817 --> 12:57.693
Yuga!

12:58.277 --> 13:00.112
I led the villains to our location.

13:01.489 --> 13:04.033
Midoriya, I am...

13:05.367 --> 13:07.161
a good-for-nothing villain.

13:09.830 --> 13:11.916
YUGA AOYAMA

13:13.501 --> 13:15.920
IZUKU MIDORIYA

13:20.424 --> 13:24.678
Unlike you, Toya, I have lots of friends.

13:24.762 --> 13:25.971
Friends, huh?

13:26.722 --> 13:30.351
Wouldn't it be a problem if it comes
to light that one of them is your friend?

13:30.434 --> 13:31.685
Not at all.

13:32.478 --> 13:35.814
If a 100-yen lighter stops working,

13:35.898 --> 13:36.941
what will you do?

13:38.108 --> 13:40.569
<i>I'm happy when my friends succeed.</i>

13:40.653 --> 13:44.657
<i>If they fail,
I'll be a little disappointed</i>

13:44.740 --> 13:47.451
<i>but simply move to a different route.</i>

13:48.536 --> 13:51.747
<i>They're nothing but disposable tools.</i>

13:52.373 --> 13:57.211
<i>If they provide any kind of excitement,
then it calls for a celebration.</i>

13:57.294 --> 13:58.921
- Yuga!
- Run!

13:59.004 --> 14:00.130
Wait!

14:01.674 --> 14:03.300
<i>Both Mama and Papa</i>

14:03.384 --> 14:06.136
<i>were greatly dismayed
because I was Quirkless.</i>

14:07.346 --> 14:09.890
<i>They were both born into wealthy families</i>

14:09.974 --> 14:12.851
<i>and led privileged lives,
never lacking anything.</i>

14:13.561 --> 14:15.604
<i>That's why I think</i>

14:15.688 --> 14:18.857
<i>the fact that I was different
worried them more than it worried me.</i>

14:19.525 --> 14:20.359
<i>That's why</i>

14:21.151 --> 14:23.028
<i>they were probably grasping at straws,</i>

14:23.737 --> 14:25.656
<i>wishing for my happiness...</i>

14:26.365 --> 14:28.909
<i>So they followed the rumors of a person</i>

14:29.410 --> 14:31.161
<i>who gives away Quirks.</i>

14:34.164 --> 14:37.793
<i>The Quirk I received disagreed
with my body, so it was tough.</i>

14:37.877 --> 14:39.420
SURPRISE!

14:40.212 --> 14:43.173
<i>But Mama and Papa experienced hardships</i>

14:43.257 --> 14:45.217
<i>in order to raise me.</i>

14:46.427 --> 14:48.804
<i>It's scary to be different from others.</i>

14:49.680 --> 14:52.433
<i>My dream began by wanting to fit in,</i>

14:53.183 --> 14:56.270
<i>but soon, it was to protect Mama and Papa
the way they protected me.</i>

14:58.439 --> 15:01.692
<i>There's a rumor that All Might
is going to become a teacher.</i>

15:01.775 --> 15:03.819
<i>Enroll him into UA High School.</i>

15:04.403 --> 15:05.321
<i>Helping others...</i>

15:06.071 --> 15:09.491
<i>Tell me when your class will be all alone.</i>

15:09.575 --> 15:11.493
<i>To make others happy...</i>

15:12.161 --> 15:14.496
<i>Tell me the location of the training camp.</i>

15:14.580 --> 15:16.749
<i>To give myself for the sake of others...</i>

15:16.832 --> 15:21.003
<i>Now that Izuku Midoriya is back
in the UA, lure him out,</i>

15:21.086 --> 15:23.047
<i>so he's alone.</i>

15:24.131 --> 15:25.466
<i>When I read your letter</i>

15:25.549 --> 15:28.427
<i>and found out that you were Quirkless
just like me,</i>

15:29.720 --> 15:31.096
I...

15:31.722 --> 15:32.681
fell into...

15:33.265 --> 15:35.809
- despair!
- Stop it, Aoyama!

15:36.769 --> 15:37.645
<i>Naval...</i>

15:38.938 --> 15:41.649
<i>- One For All...</i>
- Laser.

15:46.779 --> 15:51.367
My body has the ability to refract light.

15:53.160 --> 15:55.454
All of us could've died.

15:56.747 --> 15:59.124
All of Japan is in a chaotic mess!

16:01.126 --> 16:03.545
What were you thinking
while you were in class with us?

16:04.338 --> 16:07.257
How could you live with everyone
in the dorm, together, like that?

16:07.341 --> 16:08.968
Answer me, Aoyama!

16:09.051 --> 16:10.761
- You've got it wrong!
- Yuga is...

16:16.475 --> 16:17.434
Aoyama.

16:18.018 --> 16:19.186
Hagakure

16:19.770 --> 16:21.230
helped you,

16:21.313 --> 16:24.733
so you won't have to hurt anyone else.

16:25.776 --> 16:27.736
Let's stop this.

16:28.570 --> 16:30.739
Let's put

16:31.657 --> 16:33.200
an end to this.

16:40.082 --> 16:41.417
I see.

16:42.001 --> 16:46.880
You received a Quirk from All For One,
and he kept you under his control.

16:47.548 --> 16:50.300
The Quirk was granted
about ten years ago, huh?

16:50.884 --> 16:52.302
Since he's safe and sound,

16:52.386 --> 16:56.598
it's not like with Nagant where
it will explode with an act of betrayal.

16:56.682 --> 16:59.101
Now, I know for sure.

16:59.685 --> 17:01.979
There's a traitor.

17:02.813 --> 17:05.024
Who would've thought that
it'd be a student.

17:07.317 --> 17:08.402
Please

17:08.986 --> 17:10.612
step out for now.

17:11.196 --> 17:14.867
- Step out?
- That makes no sense.

17:15.576 --> 17:19.455
If Hagakure hadn't caught you,
what were you planning to do?

17:20.122 --> 17:21.248
Aoyama.

17:21.331 --> 17:23.417
Aoyama, tell us that it's all a lie!

17:24.001 --> 17:25.294
You were tricked, right?

17:25.878 --> 17:27.421
It wasn't on purpose, right?

17:28.380 --> 17:30.716
You used to be Quirkless too?

17:31.300 --> 17:32.885
What a small world.

17:34.219 --> 17:37.765
The sad truth is, we're still struggling
to bring order into our lives.

17:38.390 --> 17:42.269
So tell us everything you know
about All For One.

17:42.936 --> 17:45.355
We don't know anything.

17:45.939 --> 17:50.360
We only do whatever he orders us to do.

17:50.444 --> 17:54.656
If we fail, he will kill us.
If we lie, he will kill us.

17:55.324 --> 17:56.492
How do you know?

17:57.159 --> 17:58.911
He showed us

17:58.994 --> 18:01.789
how he disposes of people who fail or lie.

18:02.831 --> 18:07.419
<i>Those who went to the police
were killed after they were released.</i>

18:07.503 --> 18:09.296
<i>They couldn't escape him.</i>

18:10.047 --> 18:12.716
No matter where we go, he can find us.

18:12.800 --> 18:15.803
He will kill us for sure.

18:16.762 --> 18:18.472
Yuga only followed orders.

18:18.555 --> 18:20.390
He didn't know what would happen.

18:20.474 --> 18:23.811
He just made sure no one
would ever suspect of him.

18:24.353 --> 18:26.230
We're the ones to blame.

18:27.064 --> 18:29.191
What were you thinking
while you were in class with us?

18:31.235 --> 18:32.069
I...

18:32.820 --> 18:35.322
could've been responsible
for everyone's death.

18:36.406 --> 18:39.326
I laughed along with you guys,
pretending to be your friend.

18:40.536 --> 18:42.830
I found myself laughing with you guys.

18:43.413 --> 18:45.457
When I found out that Midoriya was once

18:45.541 --> 18:49.336
Quirkless like me but now shoulders
the heavy task of fighting All For One,

18:50.420 --> 18:53.090
I fell into despair
over my own pathetic state.

18:54.133 --> 18:55.843
<i>Instead of worrying about him,</i>

18:56.802 --> 18:58.637
<i>I was despairing over myself,</i>

18:59.429 --> 19:01.056
and that pushed me deeper into despair.

19:02.182 --> 19:05.561
I'm rotten to the core.

19:05.644 --> 19:09.231
Yuga Aoyama is a villain by nature.

19:09.314 --> 19:11.567
Then why did you

19:11.650 --> 19:14.319
<i>try to save Kacchan and Tokoyami
during the training camp?</i>

19:17.739 --> 19:18.949
And that cheese that night...

19:19.032 --> 19:19.867
I KNOW

19:19.950 --> 19:21.869
<i>Did All For One tell you to do that?</i>

19:22.870 --> 19:24.621
If all we do is face difficulties,

19:25.205 --> 19:26.748
we can never sparkle!

19:26.832 --> 19:28.458
Of course not!

19:29.918 --> 19:30.836
That was

19:31.587 --> 19:33.088
an SOS

19:33.755 --> 19:35.632
that I failed to notice!

19:36.466 --> 19:38.343
I know this because

19:39.136 --> 19:41.722
you're crying instead of making excuses,

19:42.264 --> 19:46.310
but that's not because you failed
to follow All For One's command, right?

19:47.060 --> 19:49.688
I know of a hero who was exploited
by All For One,

19:50.314 --> 19:53.233
but she still didn't give away her all.

19:54.318 --> 19:56.153
Her heart was crushed, that's all.

19:57.321 --> 19:58.739
Young Midoriya.

19:58.822 --> 20:00.449
Doing something wrong

20:00.532 --> 20:03.118
doesn't brand you as a villain forever!

20:03.952 --> 20:06.205
Take my hand,

20:06.288 --> 20:08.582
- Aoyama.
<i>- I get it now, Deku!</i>

20:09.499 --> 20:10.709
You can still

20:11.460 --> 20:13.545
be a hero!

20:14.546 --> 20:15.631
Wait, Midoriya.

20:16.173 --> 20:18.467
Sansa, cover Aoyama's mouth.

20:19.134 --> 20:21.220
He's in custody, so no hand holding.

20:21.803 --> 20:25.641
No matter the circumstance,
it's a fact that he helped All For One.

20:26.350 --> 20:29.311
<i>Plus, currently, we're can only assume
that he's safe,</i>

20:29.937 --> 20:32.481
<i>but we're not sure
if he's rigged like Nagant.</i>

20:33.357 --> 20:35.692
Until he gets tested at Central,

20:35.776 --> 20:38.362
it's not wise to let him say another word.

20:43.158 --> 20:44.576
Mr. and Mrs. Aoyama,

20:45.327 --> 20:49.289
why didn't you report to All For One
that we were going to attack Kamino?

20:50.040 --> 20:52.668
We have no way to contact All For One.

20:52.751 --> 20:55.879
Only when he has business with us

20:55.963 --> 21:00.217
does he tell us how to reach him,
but we lose contact after that.

21:00.300 --> 21:03.262
So that he can't be reached
even if you get caught.

21:03.345 --> 21:04.805
- Then...
- Mr. Tsukauchi!

21:07.099 --> 21:09.726
We can't find All For One.

21:09.810 --> 21:12.396
That's our current situation, right?

21:14.147 --> 21:16.942
Their next attack is inevitable.

21:17.025 --> 21:20.070
That's why we're trying to gather
as much manpower as we can.

21:22.155 --> 21:24.032
But we can choose...

21:24.741 --> 21:26.159
...how to enter this battle,

21:26.243 --> 21:28.829
to lure Shigaraki and the rest!

21:29.746 --> 21:30.831
That's right!

21:30.914 --> 21:33.583
If we look at this
from another perspective,

21:34.334 --> 21:36.044
Aoyama is the only one right now

21:36.128 --> 21:39.089
who can deceive All For One.

21:42.092 --> 21:44.928
Aoyama, I'll repeat myself once more.

21:46.013 --> 21:47.014
You can still

21:47.931 --> 21:49.975
be a hero!

23:21.817 --> 23:22.943
<i>Preview of the next episode.</i>

23:23.527 --> 23:27.280
<i>I know of a hero that was exploited
by All For One,</i>

23:27.364 --> 23:29.825
<i>but refused to give away her all.</i>

23:30.408 --> 23:33.870
<i>Shine light onto the heart
that has been stained with darkness.</i>

23:34.621 --> 23:38.708
<i>Even if a person falls,
they can get back up again.</i>

23:39.376 --> 23:42.504
<i>Next episode,
"The Story of How We All Became Heroes."</i>

23:43.088 --> 23:46.925
<i>Aoyama, we're not alone.</i>

23:48.009 --> 23:50.929
<i>Go Beyond. Plus Ultra!</i>

23:51.012 --> 23:51.972
Subtitle translation by: Lili Morita
